# Animations

Use **`tw-animate-css`** utility classes whenever you add UI animations (dialogs, overlays, panels, tooltips, toasts, etc.). Do **not** add custom `@keyframes` or hand-written `animation:` rules in CSS for these cases.

The package is imported in `packages/app/src/routes/layout.css`. UI components in `packages/ui` and `packages/app` rely on these utilities.

## Enter / exit (bits-ui, data-state)

Bind animations to `data-[state=open]` / `data-[state=closed]` (or equivalent state attributes):

```svelte
<div
  class={cn(
    'duration-300',
    'data-[state=closed]:animate-out data-[state=closed]:fade-out-0',
    'data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=open]:fade-in-0'
  )}
/>
```

Common combinations:

| Effect | Enter | Exit |
|--------|-------|------|
| Fade | `fade-in-0` | `fade-out-0` |
| Zoom | `zoom-in-95` | `zoom-out-95` |
| Slide from right | `slide-in-from-right` | `slide-out-to-right` |
| Slide from top | `slide-in-from-top-8` | `slide-out-to-top-8` |

Always pair `animate-in` / `animate-out` with the specific effect class. Control timing with `duration-*` and optional `delay-*` on the same element.

## Unmount timing

When a component must stay mounted until an exit animation finishes (e.g. modals), keep a `*_DURATION_MS` constant in sync with the `duration-*` class used on that element.

## When custom CSS is acceptable

- Long-running ambient/decorative loops that tw-animate-css does not cover (e.g. boot splash backgrounds).
- Do not use this exception for dialogs, overlays, slide panels, or other interactive UI motion — use tw-animate-css instead.
